{"docs":[{"description":"Larger agent systems built by combining simpler patterns, such as a research system with a lead agent and parallel searchers.","slug":"advanced","title":"Advanced Architectures"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Wrap a specialist agent as a tool, so a calling agent can hand it one bounded task and keep control.","slug":"agents-as-tools","title":"Agents as Tools"},{"description":"Common mistakes in agent systems, how to recognise them, and how to avoid them.","slug":"antipatterns","title":"Anti-Patterns"},{"cluster":"product","description":"A six-level scale for how much an agent may decide alone, chosen per kind of action from risk, not from model capability.","slug":"autonomy-ladder","title":"The Autonomy Ladder"},{"cluster":"topologies","description":"Independent specialists work on one problem through a shared workspace; a control step picks who contributes next.","slug":"blackboard","title":"Blackboard"},{"description":"Established software patterns, such as the saga, applied to agent workflows.","slug":"classical","title":"Classical Foundations"},{"description":"Ideas from cognitive science, such as self-monitoring, turned into agent patterns.","slug":"cognitive-behavioral","title":"Cognitive & Behavioral"},{"description":"How agents find and use the right information, and how to measure whether they did.","slug":"data-retrieval","title":"Data & Retrieval"},{"cluster":"advanced","description":"Split a question into parts, search them in parallel, combine the findings and check that every claim has a source.","slug":"deep-research-loop","title":"The Deep Research Loop"},{"cluster":"security","description":"Keep the model that can act away from untrusted text: a tool-less model reads it, and plain code passes results between them.","slug":"dual-llm-pattern","title":"Dual-LLM Pattern"},{"description":"Human control over autonomous systems, and their effects on people and the environment.","slug":"ethics","title":"Ethics & Sustainability"},{"description":"How to test agents and measure whether they work.","slug":"evaluation-testing","title":"Evaluation & Testing"},{"cluster":"operations-reliability","description":"Classify each failure, retry short faults with limits, switch route for lasting ones, and report reduced results honestly.","slug":"exception-handling-and-recovery","title":"Exception Handling and Recovery"},{"description":"The basic building blocks of agents, such as loops, tools and ways of combining model calls.","slug":"foundational","title":"Foundational"},{"description":"Open research questions about agents, with what is known and what is not.","slug":"future","title":"Future Research"},{"cluster":"reference-architectures","description":"A simulated character with a full memory record, reflection over it, and plans drawn from both, so it stays consistent over days.","slug":"generative-agents","title":"Generative Agents"},{"cluster":"reasoning-decision","description":"Give an agent a goal with checkable criteria, then monitor its progress and decide to continue, re-plan or stop.","slug":"goal-setting-and-monitoring","title":"Goal Setting and Monitoring"},{"description":"Records, rules and checks that make agent actions accountable.","slug":"governance","title":"Governance & Accountability"},{"cluster":"governance","description":"An append-only, hash-linked record of every important agent action, so what happened can be rebuilt and checked.","slug":"immutable-audit-log","title":"Tamper-Evident Agent Audit Log"},{"cluster":"ethics","description":"Two conditions for real human control: the system responds to relevant human reasons, and its actions trace to a person who understands it.","slug":"meaningful-human-control","title":"Meaningful Human Control"},{"description":"How agents remember, forget and turn past work into reusable skills.","slug":"memory-cognition","title":"Memory & Cognition"},{"cluster":"cognitive-behavioral","description":"A meta level watches how sure the agent 